[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706597919","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2706597919","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2706597919,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hU2gf","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T14:32:12Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T14:33:50Z","body":"One way to avoid boilerplate, while avoiding static problem, is explicitly passing a pointer that should store the value, e.g.\r\n```C++\r\nbool value = GLOBAL_GET(\"setting_name\", &some_bool_member);\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706597919/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706645574","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2706645574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2706645574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVCJG","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T14:51:15Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T14:51:50Z","body":"Quick note; I have an [open PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102126) that optimizes `GLOBAL_GET` by about 10% :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706645574/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706822619","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2706822619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2706822619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVtXb","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T15:57:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T16:27:04Z","body":"> One way to avoid boilerplate, while avoiding static problem, is explicitly passing a pointer that should store the value, e.g.\r\n> \r\n> ```c++\r\n> bool value = GLOBAL_GET(\"setting_name\", &some_bool_member);\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nSomething like that could be better, it also makes it thread safe, as the only static would need to be the local `version`, and a race condition doesn't matter there I think (worst case it would just read it e.g. two frames in a row).\r\n\r\n...\r\nActually on second thoughts, I'm not sure that helps, as it is equivalent to the existing pattern:\r\n```\r\nif (ProjectSettings::get_singleton()->has_changes()) {\r\nmy_var = GLOBAL_GET(\"my_setting\");\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo make it compatible with the existing usage we need to store the cached value somewhere, and not force the client code to manage this. Hence the use of the `static`.\r\n\r\nBut this in turn does make it non thread-safe if two threads try to update the same static cached value at the same time.. and ideally we want to do this without locks etc.\r\n\r\nMaybe we can enforce only writing to the `static` under the `ProjectSettings` lock when the version has changed. 99.9% the version won't have changed so it won't need to lock.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706822619/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706846257","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2706846257","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2706846257,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVzIx","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T16:07:20Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T16:07:20Z","body":"> > One way to avoid boilerplate, while avoiding static problem, is explicitly passing a pointer that should store the value, e.g.\r\n> > ```c++\r\n> > bool value = GLOBAL_GET(\"setting_name\", &some_bool_member);\r\n> > ```\r\n> \r\n> Something like that could be better, it also makes it thread safe, as the only static would need to be the local `version`, and a race condition doesn't matter there I think (worst case it would just read it e.g. two frames in a row).\r\n\r\nIf we're caching a variable locally anyway, we might as well cache the version locally too. Just wrap it in `struct SettingsCache` and store that instead of a plain variable. Call `.get()` on it when you access it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706846257/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706988008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2706988008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2706988008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hWVvo","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T17:14:47Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T17:15:10Z","body":"This makes me wonder if a GDScript equivalent should exist too, but it's probably easier to just document this in the class reference and show an example of cached usage.\r\n\r\nAlso, should `EDITOR_GET` have an equivalent macro?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706988008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2707063640","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2707063640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2707063640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hWoNY","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T17:54:46Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T17:54:46Z","body":"OK I've taken on board the suggestions above, and refined a bit .. I'm sure there will be more bikeshedding.\r\n\r\n* I've used @Ivorforce suggestion to pass the type to the macro, and use an `is_trivially_destructible` assert to prevent `Variants` (the constructible check doesn't allow `Color`, which is actually fine, as would be e.g. `Vector3` etc .. the problem is more that `Variants` create secondary memory etc).\r\n* Although ultimately I agree that it would be a good idea to have the regular `GLOBAL_GET` use the cache, and have the old version named `GLOBAL_GET_UNCACHED`, I've left it the other way around here in the interest of making reviewing the PR easier. It's easy to swap these round in a follow up PR.\r\n* I've managed to make it (I think) thread safe by storing a mutex used globally in the `ProjectSettings`. 99.9% of the time the version won't change so it won't need to touch the mutex.\r\n* For the concerns for the string parameter invoking costs, I've changed the `StringName` to `const char *` as all the calling sites are `const char *`. I'm a lambda newbie (c++98 FTW) so would probably prefer to have that approach spelled out to me or else leave that to a follow up by someone more versed in lambdas.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2707063640/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2707067318","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2707067318","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2707067318,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hWpG2","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T17:57:01Z","updated_at":"2025-03-08T08:28:31Z","body":"> Also, should EDITOR_GET have an equivalent macro?\r\n\r\nVery probably. I've not used it much as I mostly deal with runtime bottlenecks, but I don't think there's any harm in making the editor snappier too.\r\n\r\nProbably for another PR though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2707067318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733483537","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2733483537","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2733483537,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6i7aYR","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-18T14:35:06Z","updated_at":"2025-03-18T14:35:06Z","body":"Ok is modified to take care of the case when the function calling `GET_GLOBAL_CACHED()` is re-entrant as is reading from the cached version at the same time as writing.\r\n\r\n@Ivorforce has provided version which avoids the mutex and we've tested as 3x faster than a simple mutex version.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733483537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733620104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2733620104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2733620104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6i77uI","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-18T15:13:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-18T15:40:47Z","body":"Calling @RandomShaper to help with the atomics.\r\n\r\nI'm really not qualified for this area, the smallest thing I deal with is a mutex. :grin: \r\nI suspect the compilation error is because the atomic we are trying to use here is bigger than the CPU native types?\r\n\r\nFor future reference, linking errors were like:\r\n```\r\n/usr/include/c++/11/atomic:285: undefined reference to `__atomic_load_16'\r\n/usr/bin/ld: drivers/libdrivers.x11.opt.tools.64.a(rasterizer_gles2.x11.opt.tools.64.o): in function `std::atomic<Pair<unsigned int, double> >::store(Pair<unsigned int, double>, std::memory_order)':\r\n/usr/include/c++/11/atomic:271: undefined reference to `__atomic_store_16'\r\n/usr/bin/ld: drivers/libdrivers.x11.opt.tools.64.a(rasterizer_gles2.x11.opt.tools.64.o): in function `std::atomic<Pair<unsigned int, double> >::load(std::memory_order) const':\r\n/usr/include/c++/11/atomic:285: undefined reference to `__atomic_load_16'\r\n/usr/bin/ld: editor/libeditor.x11.opt.tools.64.a(theme_editor_preview.x11.opt.tools.64.o): in function `std::atomic<Pair<unsigned int, Color> >::store(Pair<unsigned int, Color>, std::memory_order)':\r\n/usr/include/c++/11/atomic:271: undefined reference to `__atomic_store'\r\n/usr/bin/ld: editor/libeditor.x11.opt.tools.64.a(theme_editor_preview.x11.opt.tools.64.o): in function `std::atomic<Pair<unsigned int, Color> >::load(std::memory_order) const':\r\n/usr/include/c++/11/atomic:285: undefined reference to `__atomic_load'\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt may be possible to do in a slightly different way and still gain the speed advantage over a mutex (3x faster than mutex), but even if not, I'm happy to revert to using a mutex if we can't do with atomics, as it's still loads faster than before.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733620104/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733990424","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103763#issuecomment-2733990424","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103763","id":2733990424,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6i9WIY","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-18T16:47:21Z","updated_at":"2025-03-18T16:47:21Z","body":"Thanks be to the gods. :+1: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2733990424/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]